      "content": "The data does indicate a statistically minor elevation in reported nausea, but we have supporting secondary data showing that 90% of those cases were self-limiting and resolved within the first six hours of treatment. We can leverage the pharmacokinetic profile to argue that the nausea is transient and directly related to the rapid absorption, which is the very mechanism driving our superior action. This allows us to position the drug as a powerful, fast-acting solution where the initial discomfort is a temporary trade-off for immediate, profound pain relief.",
